{"question_id": "8a2466db", "hypothesis": "Based on our previous conversation, here are the resources I recommended for learning more about video editing, specifically with Adobe Premiere Pro:\n\n## Recommended Resources\n\n**Official Documentation & Tutorials:**\n- Adobe Premiere Pro's official documentation and tutorials\n\n**YouTube Channels:**\n- **Premiere Bro** \u2013 a channel dedicated to Premiere Pro tips and techniques\n- **Video Copilot** \u2013 creates content about Adobe Premiere Pro (and was also mentioned for their Orb plugin)\n- **Adobe Creative Cloud** \u2013 Adobe's official channel with tutorials and creative content\n\n**Online Course Platforms:**\n- **Udemy** \u2013 offers various video editing courses\n- **LinkedIn Learning** \u2013 offers courses specifically on Adobe Premiere Pro\n- **Skillshare** \u2013 another platform with video editing classes\n\n**Communities & Forums:**\n- **Reddit's r/premierepro** \u2013 a community for Premiere Pro users to share tips and ask questions\n- **Adobe's Premiere Pro forum** \u2013 official forum for troubleshooting and discussion\n\nSince you mentioned you enjoy using Adobe Premiere Pro and have been particularly interested in the Lumetri Color Panel and color grading, these resources should serve you well. The YouTube channels and online courses would be especially helpful for visual, step-by-step learning, while the forums are great for getting answers to specific questions as you continue to practice and experiment with advanced features.", "verdict": "yes", "question_type": "single-session-preference"}
