{"question_id": "6222b6eb", "hypothesis": "Based on our previous conversation on May 21, 2023, the **6S** algorithm (Second Simulation of a Satellite Signal in the Solar Spectrum) is the one implemented in the **SIAC_GEE** tool.\n\nSpecifically, as I mentioned in that conversation:\n\n> \"6S (Second Simulation of a Satellite Signal in the Solar Spectrum) algorithm, is a radiative transfer model that simulates the interactions between electromagnetic radiation and the Earth's atmosphere, land, and water surfaces. It is implemented in the SIAC_GEE (Sentinel-2 Image Atmospheric Correction in Google Earth Engine) tool.\"\n\nTo recap the three algorithms we discussed:\n- **6S** \u2192 implemented in **SIAC_GEE** (runs on Google Earth Engine)\n- **MAJA** \u2192 implemented in MAJA software (developed by CNES, the French Space Agency)\n- **Sen2Cor** \u2192 implemented in Sen2Cor software (developed by ESA)\n\nSo the answer to your question is **6S**.", "verdict": "yes", "question_type": "single-session-assistant"}
